   "publish_time_utc": "2026-11-10 02:24:43",
   "text": "I am shaking right now...🤯\n\nI gave Fable 5.2 (max) a single prompt: \"build a hyper-realistic first person shooter set on a tropical island, AAA quality visuals and sound effects, make no mistakes\" and let it run unattended.\n\nThe result looks absolutely stunning. Everything procedural in raw WebGPU, no engine.\n\nHere are the actual telemetry stats from the run:\n- Consumed 179 million tokens across 27 autonomous sub-agents over a continuous 9 hour run\n- Rendering ~30 million polygons per frame with real-time subsurface scattering on every palm frond\n- Y-axis heightmaps and coastal erosion patterns generated procedurally using 4K compute shaders\n- Self-verified 124K output tokens of custom GLSL shaders using its internal headless browser loop to fix shadow-map acne\n- Instanced 4,200 destuctible bamboo huts and rigid-body physics barrels at a locked 60 FPS\n- Simulated volumetric god-rays, ocean FFT wave dynamics, and inverse kinematics\n\nTraditional AAA game studios are officially cooked",
